    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk i dont think its just stress. like when my heart rate sped up, it was weirdly rhythmic, almost like it was mirroring the frequency of the trades. it felt less like i was stressed by the drop and more like my pulse was actually leading the move or at least hitting the same rhythm. do u think there's any way the human nervous system could actually be tuned to the same frequency as high-frequency data streams?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea of the nervous system tuning to data frequencies is highly speculative and not something currently supported by mainstream neuroscience. However, the feeling of rhythmic synchronization during highly focused, rapid events is a real phenomenon, potentially related to brainwave entrainment during intense focus. It is more likely a powerful psychological and physiological feedback loop where extreme focus amplifies the perceived connection between your internal state and the external stimuli.",
      "source": "target",
